# Consumers of this package (data-retrieved, data-transformed, ...) install it
# as a git dependency and only ever run the pipeline code. The Polly HTTP
# recordings and snapshots under tests/ are ~1.2GB, which every CI job was
# downloading and unpacking on every run for no reason. Excluding them takes the
# installed package from ~1166MB to ~1MB.
tests/

# Generated output directories. LEADING SLASHES ARE REQUIRED: an unanchored
# pattern like `cache/` matches at every level and would also drop the
# `scripts/cache/` pipeline stage. These only ever exist at the package root, so
# anchor them there. npm uses this file *instead of* .gitignore when packing, so
# these are repeated from .gitignore to keep a local `npm pack` clean (git-dep
# installs pack from a clean checkout and never see them anyway).
/transformed-data/
/retrieved-data/
/combined-data/
/matched-data/
/cached-data/
/cache-llm/
/cache/
/playwright-failures/

# local tooling
/.claude/
/.env
*.log
*.tgz
